Reasoning:
My Spring 1901 orders are straightforward and align with all existing agreements. A BUD moves to Serbia, which is unoccupied and uncontested by Turkey (who is taking Bulgaria). This secures a build for Fall 1901. A VIE moves to Galicia, as communicated to Russia; they acknowledged "Gal/Ser ok" but didn't explicitly promise to stay out, so a bounce with A WAR is possible but acceptable—if bounced, I hold. F TRI moves to Albania, consistent with the Italy DMZ (no ADR or TYR moves) and positions me for a future push into Greece. No supports are needed since all target provinces are unoccupied. These moves honor all pacts and set up expansion.

